The decision by the mayor and council to approve in whole or part, to reject, to place conditions upon, or to delete a application for a grant shall be based on, but not limited to, a consideration of the following criteria:
(a) Whether the project shall benefit and enhance the health, public safety, and general welfare of the residents and businesses of the city and the community improvement district;
(b) Whether the project shall be consistent with, and beneficial to, the land uses in the vicinity of the proposed project, as the property is currently being used or as may be anticipated under the official land use plan of the city;
(c) Whether the project presents a prudent and rational use of the resources of the commission in light of the available amount of commission revenues, the degree of benefit to the citizens of the community improvement district and nature and necessity of other grant requests;
(d) Whether the project shall contribute to the reduction of traffic, noise, water pollution, air pollution, noise pollution, or other effects of increased development within the community improvement district;
(e) Whether the project shall enhance the aesthetic appearance of properties, land, buildings, or other structures within the community improvement district;
(f) Whether the project shall benefit and enhance the quality of life within the community improvement district through the promotion and support of the arts, recreation, or leisure activities of the citizens within the community improvement district.
(Ord. of 8-2-1999)

